nc-vehicle-gear-r = R
nc-vehicle-lever-state = Column { $column }: { $row } · { $reverse }
nc-vehicle-reverse-armed = Reverse latch open
nc-vehicle-reverse-locked = Reverse latch closed
nc-vehicle-exit = Exit
nc-vehicle-controls = Q: throttle · E: brake · Shift: clutch · Space: handbrake · WASD: gear lever
nc-vehicle-pedals = Throttle { $gas }% · Brake { $brake }% · Clutch pressed { $clutch }%
nc-vehicle-shift-clutch-required = Shift rejected: press the clutch (Shift) before moving the lever into gear.
nc-vehicle-shift-waiting = Waiting for the clutch pedal to finish travelling — keep Shift held.
nc-vehicle-shift-neutral = Neutral: the engine is disconnected from the wheels. A/D only select the lever gate.
nc-vehicle-shift-engaged = Gear engaged.
nc-vehicle-launch-manual = Start the engine in N and wait for RPM. First gear: hold Shift → A → W → hold Q and release Shift. Release Space (handbrake).
    Reverse: stop → Neutral → hold Shift → press Reverse (latch) → D to column 3 → S. Once R appears above, hold Q and release Shift.
nc-vehicle-ignition-start = Start engine
nc-vehicle-ignition-stop = Stop engine
nc-vehicle-engine-stopped = Engine stopped. Select Neutral and press Start engine.
nc-vehicle-engine-cranking = Starter turning. Wait for the engine to start; pressing again cancels starting.
nc-vehicle-engine-running = Engine running.
nc-vehicle-engine-high-rpm = High RPM: shift up. The limiter cuts power and sustained running gradually wears the engine.
nc-vehicle-launch-release-clutch = Engine running, clutch pressed: hold Q and release Shift to move.
nc-vehicle-launch-handbrake = Handbrake applied: release Space to move.
nc-vehicle-start-driver = Starting blocked: the driver must be conscious and seated.
nc-vehicle-start-cargo = Starting blocked: secure the vehicle on the recovery bed.
nc-vehicle-start-key = Starting blocked: hold this vehicle's key in a hand.
nc-vehicle-start-fuel = Starting blocked: the fuel tank is empty.
nc-vehicle-start-assembly = Starting blocked: required engine or transmission parts are missing or disconnected. Check the assembly in the workshop.
nc-vehicle-start-selector = Starting blocked: select P or N.
nc-vehicle-start-clutch = Starting blocked: select Neutral or fully press the clutch (Shift).
nc-vehicle-start-burning = Starting blocked: extinguish the vehicle first.
nc-vehicle-start-starter-fault = Starting blocked: the starter circuit is disconnected or broken. Check the starter, battery and wiring.
nc-vehicle-start-ignition-fault = Starting blocked: the ignition circuit is disconnected or broken. Check the ignition parts, fuel pump and wiring.
nc-vehicle-start-overheated = Starting blocked: let the engine cool down.
nc-vehicle-start-battery = Starting blocked: insufficient battery charge for the starter.
nc-vehicle-launch-automatic = Starting: ignition in P/N → select D with S → throttle with Q. W/S move the P–R–N–D–L selector.
nc-vehicle-telemetry = { $speed } km/h · { $rpm } RPM · Gear: { $gear } · { $fuel } L

